---
import './figure.css';
import './session-card.css';
---

<figure class="post-fig f7" aria-describedby="f7-desc">
  <figcaption>
    <p class="post-fig-title">figure 3: from tool result to note</p>
    <p class="muted">
      The agent's replies are input to the note, not the note: they lean on the log, and some
      hold guesses that do not survive.
    </p>
  </figcaption>
  <div id="f7-desc" class="sr-only"><slot /></div>

  <div class="step">
    <section class="sess" aria-label="step 1, raw tool result">
      <header class="sess-h"><span>1 raw tool result</span><b>t4..t5</b></header>
      <ol class="sess-b">
        <li class="ln">
          <span class="who">agent</span><span class="msg">$ pnpm build</span>
        </li>
        <li class="ln tool">
          <span class="who">tool</span>
          <div class="msg res log">
            <div>&gt; place@0.1.0 build</div>
            <div>&gt; tsc -p .</div>
            <div class="err">
              src/client/api.ts(12,5): error TS2322: Type 'string' is not assignable to type
              'number'.
            </div>
            <div>src/client/api.ts(31,5): error TS2322: Type 'string' is not assignable …</div>
            <div>src/client/api.ts(48,3): error TS2741: Property 'cursor' is missing …</div>
            <div class="cm">(400 more lines)</div>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>
    <dl class="side">
      <dt>size</dt>
      <dd class="num">~400 lines</dd>
      <dt>fate</dt>
      <dd>stays in archive</dd>
    </dl>
  </div>

  <p class="arrow">the agent replies to it, round by round</p>

  <div class="step">
    <section class="sess" aria-label="step 2, the agent's replies mid-episode">
      <header class="sess-h"><span>2 the agent's replies, mid-episode</span><b>t6..t10</b></header>
      <ol class="sess-b">
        <li class="ln">
          <span class="who">agent</span><span class="msg"
            ><span class="guess">change the field type in src/client/api.ts by hand</span>{' '}
            <span class="cm">(rejected later)</span></span
          >
        </li>
        <li class="ln user">
          <span class="who">user</span><span class="msg">don't edit generated files</span>
        </li>
        <li class="ln">
          <span class="who">agent</span><span class="msg"
            >the errors are all in the generated client, regenerating it</span
          >
        </li>
        <li class="ln">
          <span class="who">agent</span><span class="msg">$ pnpm generate &amp;&amp; pnpm build</span>
        </li>
        <li class="ln tool">
          <span class="who">tool</span><span class="msg res"
            ><span class="ok">✓</span> done in 41s</span
          >
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p class="sess-f">
        replies lean on the output above ("the errors"); the first guess did not survive
      </p>
    </section>
    <dl class="side">
      <dt>size</dt>
      <dd class="num">~40 tokens</dd>
      <dt>fate</dt>
      <dd>input to the note</dd>
    </dl>
  </div>

  <p class="arrow">build passes · fold(since: "t4")</p>

  <div class="step">
    <section class="sess wide" aria-label="step 3, the note at fold time">
      <header class="sess-h">
        <span>3 note at fold time</span><b>fold(since: "t4", note) -&gt; <span class="hd">"b2e4"</span></b>
      </header>
      <ol class="sess-b note">
        <li class="ln">
          <span class="who">changed</span><span class="msg"
            >regenerated src/client from the OpenAPI spec, no source edits</span
          >
        </li>
        <li class="ln">
          <span class="who">learned</span><span class="msg"
            >regenerating the stale client fixed the build errors</span
          >
        </li>
        <li class="ln">
          <span class="who">rejected</span><span class="msg"
            >editing <code>src/client/api.ts</code> by hand (overwritten on next generate)</span
          >
        </li>
        <li class="ln">
          <span class="who">open</span><span class="msg"
            >does CI run generate before build? unchecked</span
          >
        </li>
        <li class="ln">
          <span class="who">where</span><span class="msg">thread <span class="hd">b2e4</span></span>
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p class="sess-f">stands on its own; quotes the exact path for later lookups</p>
    </section>
    <dl class="side">
      <dt>size</dt>
      <dd class="num">~60 tokens</dd>
      <dt>fate</dt>
      <dd>the note</dd>
    </dl>
  </div>
</figure>

<style>

  /* fig 7 */
  .f7 .step {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 17ch;
    gap: 0 16px;
    align-items: start;
  }
  .f7 .wide .ln {
    grid-template-columns: 8ch minmax(0, 1fr);
  }
  .f7 .side {
    margin: 0;
    padding-top: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--comment-ink);
  }
  .f7 .side dt {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    clip-path: inset(50%);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .f7 .side dd {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .f7 .side .num {
    font-size: 13px;
  }
  .f7 .arrow {
    margin: 2px 0 2px 3ch;
    padding: 2px 0 2px 12px;
    border-left: 1px dashed var(--rule);
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--comment-ink);
  }
  .f7 .arrow::before {
    content: '↓ ';
    color: var(--muted-ink);
  }
  .f7 .log > div {
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .f7 .log .err {
    color: var(--loop);
  }
  .f7 .guess {
    text-decoration: underline wavy var(--loop);
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  .f7 code {
    padding: 0 3px;
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--metric-ink) 18%, transparent);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: inherit;
  }
  .f7 .sess-f::before {
    content: '↑ ';
  }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .f7 .step {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
    .f7 .side {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 0 12px;
    }
  }
</style>
